### Part 1: The Prompt to Paste into Google AI Studio

Paste this exact prompt into the Google AI Studio app prompt input:

```markdown
Build a comprehensive, production-grade Universal Storage & Database Management Dashboard in React with Tailwind CSS and Express/Node.js backend.

The application must support 9 complete storage architectures:
1. Firebase / Cloud Firestore (NoSQL)
2. Cloud SQL / Self-hosted PostgreSQL & MySQL (Relational SQL via pg/mysql2)
3. Serverless SQL (Neon Postgres / PlanetScale)
4. Hosted NoSQL (MongoDB Atlas)
5. Google Workspace API (Google Sheets API v4 append, read, clear)
6. Vector Database (Pinecone / Chroma API for embedding upsert and cosine similarity query)
7. Google Cloud Storage (GCS) & Firebase Storage (Signed URLs, bucket upload, list, download)
8. S3-Compatible Object Storage (AWS S3 / Cloudflare R2 / MinIO via @aws-sdk/client-s3)
9. Client-Side Browser Storage (IndexedDB via Dexie.js + LocalStorage)

Features for each storage engine:
- Connection Status Pill (Connected / Disconnected / Testing / Latency in ms)
- Interactive Control Panel with 5 dedicated action buttons:
  * "Test Ping / Health Check"
  * "Insert Sample Record / Write"
  * "Query / Fetch Records"
  * "Full JSON Backup (Download Snapshot)"
  * "Restore from Backup (Upload & Overwrite/Merge)"
- Interactive Data Inspector: Live table and raw JSON explorer displaying fetched/inserted records.
- Config Drawer / Modal: Allows updating credentials (URI, API Keys, Tokens, Service Account keys) with sensible defaults or mock fallback mode so every button executes immediately with realistic latency without breaking.
- Notification Toast System: Instant feedback displaying status codes, response payloads, execution time, and error traces.
- Clean responsive dark-mode UI with Lucide-react icons, tabs for switching between engines, and a global "Test All Connections" master button.

```

